u and he's got about maybe  it's hard to gauge but maybe fifty  thousand followers he directed Trekkies  as well which is celebrated for  quirky characters who are the new  Nygaard characters that are coming out  this time  well that's the thing is it's the topic  is less important in a good documentary  than finding interesting people to talk  about the topic there's a guru named aha  for instance who you've probably never  seen anything like him he's he is he's  the type of person people go to and ask  questions and he answers questions he's  it looks a little bit like Harry Knowles  of a Nakul nose you know so he's got a  unique look but you wouldn't necessarily  expect him to be you know mr. wisdom but  when you listen to what he says what he  says is really interesting and usually  pretty down-to-earth so you must be a  much wiser man now than you were at the  beginning of this you mentioned advice  what kind of pearls of wisdom can you  toss our way I changed me dramatically  actually I mean imagine talking to a  hundred and you know fifteen hundred  seventy people many of which were  psychologists spending two hours with a  psychologist asking him the toughest  questions that are keeping you up at  night all for free we all search for  happiness that's one thing people say I  just want to be happy I want to find  happiness I want to find somebody  that'll make me happy  well you can't search for happiness it's  one thing I learned happiness and I'm  quoting Julia Sweeney now that's what  she said in the movie happiness is a  byproduct of having a purpose in order  to get happiness you need to have a  reason for being now how do you find  your purpose how do you find your reason  for being well a lot of people feel like  when I've talked to them there's some  they're searching for some big complex  answer that explains everything but the  answer what I found is so simple that's  why it's hard to see and one thing AHA  said when in one of his seminar is a  woman stood up and said I don't know  where to find my purpose I don't know  where to look and he said I hate to be  the one to break it to you but your  purpose is that person right next to you  on your left and that person on your  right that's your purpose we're we're  social creatures and we find our purpose  and thus our happiness in our social  interactions with friends and family did  you find that some types of people  tended  be happier than others I interviewed a  guy at Harvard his name is Daniel  Gilbert he's a professor of psychology  and he wrote a book called stumbling  unhappiness and he studied happiness for  years and one of the questions that came  up he told me is who was happier in life  and what the studies showed was that  we're all pretty equally happy in jail  on average no matter who you if you  compare it to someone who is disabled  versus someone who's not people have an  equal capacity for happiness did you  find more more or less happiness  religious people versus atheists yes  there is there've been studies done on  that and what they have found is that  religious people tend to be a little bit  happier than non-religious people but  that also has to do with having a social  group that you're a part of that's what  brings you happiness is having a group  of people that you're a part of who want  to know about you listen to you talk to  you care about what you're doing and you  spoke with the prominent atheist Richard  Dawkins what did he have to say Richard  Dawkins is he's one of the best  interviews you can do because he's  everything he says is quotable because  he's definitive he will tell you what he  thinks and with unequivocably and he's  he's the Pope of atheists it's been  roughly a decade since Trekkies how has  the the film market changed since then  the indie film market is continually  changing because now it's what's gotten  much worse and much better for in  different ways it's much harder to  release a film through the traditional  methods because most of the distribution  companies have been bought up by  corporations and so they're all swinging  for the fence with blockbusters they're  much less interested in a nice clean  single there's a few companies left that  are still doing that and new ones come  and go but it's not like it used to be  however you can now put your movie on  YouTube and so many other internet  avenues that you can bypass those  traditional methods of release short  films now there are people making a lot  of money on the internet making short  films  and putting it on YouTube or whatever  and and making money off the advertising  that's their job and everybody says you  know well you've got to harness that new  media stuff and it sounds like a just a  platitude but you seem to have done some  pretty creative things in that regard  that I assume are actually working can  you talk about that and how our viewers  can can see what you've done  well part of releasing a film is you've  got to put little pieces out there get  people interested get them a little bit  pregnant in in wanting to see your film  so we've been putting out webisodes  outtakes excerpts special pieces of  footage that I found in the raw footage  and publishing those on the internet and  on our website which is the nature of  existence calm what's the the status of  your film network and people see it it's  done the festival circuit already yeah  we do your film festivals won some  awards and now it's being released  theatrically in movie theaters our  website will list all of the show times  and locations and then home video of  course home video will be it's still  evolving but what we're planning to do  with home video is released the  documentary on DVD as well as we're  creating a seven disc companion set of  all these topics in much greater depth  and detail for those who really want to  probe more deeply on the nature of  existence where it is there an afterlife  where is it located what